1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,607
How does a card number stay safe on its way to the bank?

2
00:00:02,607 --> 00:00:07,464
The simplest way is that the store's website collects the card number and sends it to the bank.

3
00:00:07,464 --> 00:00:14,380
But then every store holds card data, and under PCI DSS that makes each one a target and a liability.

4
00:00:14,380 --> 00:00:19,952
So the card is entered only on the bank's hosted payment page, opened by a one-time session link.

5
00:00:19,952 --> 00:00:25,964
The bank's token vault turns the card number into a token, and the payment keeps only a masked PAN.

6
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:30,452
The real number is revealed only inside the bank, at the moment of the debit.

7
00:00:30,452 --> 00:00:36,047
To prove the payer owns the card, a one-time password goes by SMS to the card's phone.

8
00:00:36,047 --> 00:00:41,130
Resends are limited and spaced by the configured time, and wrong attempts are limited too.

